      "kind": "source",
      "file": "src/h3lib/lib/polyfill.c",
      "function": "maxPolygonToCellsSizeExperimental",
      "line": 759,
      "code": "iter._flags = CONTAINMENT_OVERLAPPING_BBOX;",
      "note": "maxPolygonToCellsSizeExperimental unconditionally overrides the iterator's containment mode to CONTAINMENT_OVERLAPPING_BBOX for size estimation, regardless of the caller's requested flags. For the PoC polygon, the OVERLAPPING_BBOX mode produces an undercount because it lacks the cellBoundaryCrossesPolygon check that CONTAINMENT_OVERLAPPING has."
    },
    {
      "kind": "root_cause_function",
      "file": "src/h3lib/lib/polyfill.c",
      "function": "iterStepPolygonCompact",
      "line": null,
      "code": "else if (mode == CONTAINMENT_OVERLAPPING &&",
      "note": "The cellBoundaryCrossesPolygon line-intersection check in iterStepPolygonCompact only fires when mode == CONTAINMENT_OVERLAPPING, excluding CONTAINMENT_OVERLAPPING_BBOX. Since maxPolygonToCellsSizeExperimental forces OVERLAPPING_BBOX mode for size estimation, boundary-crossing cells are not counted by the fine-grained check. The OVERLAPPING_BBOX fallback block at line 519 uses a coarser bbox-based approximation that can miss cells. The fix adds mode == CONTAINMENT_OVERLAPPING_BBOX to this condition, ensuring the size estimate is a superset of what any mode can produce."
    },
